        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. France 'very unhelpful': Trump lashes out at allies Issued on: 01/04/2026 - 11:36 President Donald Trump expressed frustration Tuesday with allies who have been unwilling to do more to support the US war effort, telling them to “go get your own oil” as the conflict with Iran and its closure of the Strait of Hormuz sent average US gas prices past $4 a gallon. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi tells us more. The latest from Tehran: 'Airstrikes hit non-military targets every day' 01/04/2026 Lebanon says Israeli strikes on Beirut area kill 7 01/04/2026 US Supreme Court rules against ban on 'conversion therapy' for LGBTQ minors 01/04/2026 'Massive disappointment': Italy at new low after missing out on yet another World Cup 01/04/2026 Death penalty 'a deep stain on the law books of the state of Israel' 01/04/2026 Middle East ‘Blatantly racist’: Death penalty law among 'worst legislation' in Israeli parliamentary history 01/04/2026 Middle East 'Gravest crime against humanity: Brazil still suffers from effects of slavery' 01/04/2026 Americas As US pursues 'maximalist demands', Iran relies on four decades of asymmetric warfare 01/04/2026 Middle East EU faces 'largest oil supply disruption in history', energy expert says 31/03/2026 Europe"
